Boost 1.92.0 headers are statically compiled into this core. The checked
source slice is native/geometry/vendor/boost-geometry-1.92.0.tar.gz.
The initial capture uses the unmodified installed Homebrew Boost headers;
every copied file is individually checksum pinned. Homebrew identifies the
upstream source as:
https://github.com/boostorg/boost/releases/download/boost-1.92.0/boost-1.92.0-b2-nodocs.tar.xz
SHA-256 ea7b982002cc9dfbe59b0b217b206f470dc75f3de0bb2973d844118934d82411
That upstream archive checksum identifies the original source release;
the checked source-slice checksum is separately recorded in the manifest.
Boost files preserve their original authors' notices and BSL-1.0 terms;
see BOOST-LICENSE. No compiled Boost library is linked.

The build preserves conditional platform headers and expands modules that
compute include filenames, so it does not rely on the developer's installed
headers. The generated export/configuration headers describe static linking
and the selected upstream geometry options. The unused SMILES JSON settings
translation unit is excluded; no numerical geometry implementation is
substituted or approximated. Neither Python nor a downloaded executable is
part of this native core or its runtime.
